      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 12 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 16 & 0 \\\\ -26 & -40 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{33}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 12 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 16 & 0 \\\\ -8 & -4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}+9R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 16 & 0 \\\\ -26 & -40 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}+9R_{3}$.",
